{%- comment -%}
  Per-section colour control.

  Emits a style block scoped to one section that re-points the design tokens
  for that section only. Because the sections are built on tokens rather than
  hard-coded colours, moving the tokens moves headings, body text, rules,
  eyebrows, buttons and cards together, instead of leaving half a section on
  the old palette.

  Text colour is measured, not guessed. Shopify's color_contrast filter gives
  the real ratio, so the snippet picks whichever of the light or dark text
  ramps actually reads on the ground the merchant chose, and says so in the
  theme editor when even the better option falls under AA. A colour picker
  that lets somebody publish cream text on a cream ground is not a feature.

  Required
    id       section.id
  Optional
    scheme   one of: default, cream, oat, forest, gold, clay, custom
    bg       ground colour, custom scheme only
    accent   button and link colour, custom scheme only
    tone     auto, dark or light. Auto measures. Default auto.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = scheme | default: 'default'

  case s
    when 'cream'
      assign ground = '#FAF6EF'
      assign acc = '#2C4A3E'
    when 'oat'
      assign ground = '#F1E9DB'
      assign acc = '#2C4A3E'
    when 'forest'
      assign ground = '#1A2B24'
      assign acc = '#C9943A'
    when 'gold'
      assign ground = '#F5EAD6'
      assign acc = '#805E20'
    when 'clay'
      assign ground = '#2C4A3E'
      assign acc = '#C9943A'
    when 'custom'
      assign ground = bg
      assign acc = accent | default: '#2C4A3E'
  endcase
-%}
{%- if s != 'default' and ground != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    comment
      Measure both ramps against the ground and take the winner. The numbers
      are the real ratio, so "light" is chosen because it reads, not because
      the colour looked dark in the picker.
    endcomment
    assign dark_ink = '#17150F'
    assign light_ink = '#FAF6EF'
    assign c_dark = ground | color_contrast: dark_ink
    assign c_light = ground | color_contrast: light_ink

    assign auto_light = false
    if c_light > c_dark
      assign auto_light = true
    endif
    assign auto_best = c_dark
    if auto_light
      assign auto_best = c_light
    endif

    assign use_light = auto_light
    if tone == 'dark'
      assign use_light = false
    elsif tone == 'light'
      assign use_light = true
    endif

    assign best = c_dark
    if use_light
      assign best = c_light
    endif

    comment
      A forced tone is respected right up to the point where it stops being a
      choice and becomes a mistake. Light text on a cream ground measures
      1:1, which is not a look, it is an invisible section. Below AA, and only
      when the measured option is genuinely better, the readable one wins and
      the editor explains why. Anything merely close to the line is left alone.
    endcomment
    assign overridden = false
    if best < 4.5 and auto_best > best
      assign use_light = auto_light
      assign best = auto_best
      assign overridden = true
    endif

    comment
      Same test for the button: the label takes whichever of cream or near
      black reads on the accent the merchant picked.
    endcomment
    assign ac_dark = acc | color_contrast: dark_ink
    assign ac_light = acc | color_contrast: light_ink
    assign on_acc = dark_ink
    if ac_light > ac_dark
      assign on_acc = light_ink
    endif

    if use_light
      assign ink = '#FAF6EF'
      assign ink2 = '#D8E2DC'
      assign ink3 = '#A9BBB1'
    else
      assign ink = '#17150F'
      assign ink2 = '#453D2F'
      assign ink3 = '#5E5442'
    endif

    comment
      Surfaces and rules are mixed from the ground itself rather than being
      translucent overlays, so they stay solid wherever they land and keep
      their relationship to the background whatever it is set to.
    endcomment
    assign surface = ground | color_mix: ink, 95
    assign rule = ground | color_mix: ink, 82
  -%}
  <style>
    /* The id beats both the base tokens on .pl.pl and the cooling colourway
       on .pl.pl.pl, so an explicit choice in the editor always wins. */
    #shopify-section-{{ id }} .pl.pl {
      --bone: {{ ground }};
      --oat: {{ surface }};
      --sand: {{ rule }};
      --ink: {{ ink }};
      --ink-2: {{ ink2 }};
      --ink-3: {{ ink3 }};
      --clay: {{ acc }};
      --clay-dk: {{ acc }};
      --clay-onDark: {{ acc }};
      --on-dark-lede: {{ ink2 }};
      --on-dark-body: {{ ink3 }};
    }
    #shopify-section-{{ id }} .pl .pl-section,
    #shopify-section-{{ id }} .pl .pl-section--oat,
    #shopify-section-{{ id }} .pl .pl-section--dark { background: {{ ground }}; }
    /* The scrim over a background photograph is the section's own ground at
       partial opacity, so a merchant who changes the scheme gets a scrim that
       still matches — and text whose measured contrast is against the colour
       actually behind it. */
    #shopify-section-{{ id }} .pl .finale-bg::after { background: {{ ground }}; }
    /* The solid button re-declares its own label colour, so it needs saying
       here. Ghost and on-dark variants already track --ink and --sand, which
       moved with the tokens above, so they are left alone. */
    #shopify-section-{{ id }} .pl .btn:not(.btn--ghost):not(.btn--onDark) { --btn-fg: {{ on_acc }}; }
    #shopify-section-{{ id }} .pl .eyebrow { color: {{ ink3 }}; }
  </style>
  {%- if request.design_mode -%}
    {%- if overridden -%}
      <p style="margin:0;padding:.6rem 1rem;background:#7A1F1F;color:#fff;font:14px/1.4 system-ui">
        Colour check: {{ tone }} text on this background measures under 4.5:1, so the
        readable option is being used instead. Change the background if you want
        {{ tone }} text here.
      </p>
    {%- elsif best < 4.5 -%}
      <p style="margin:0;padding:.6rem 1rem;background:#7A1F1F;color:#fff;font:14px/1.4 system-ui">
        Colour check: the best available text colour reaches only {{ best }}:1 on this
        background. AA needs 4.5:1 for body text. Pick a lighter or darker background.
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
